mapping "b761.1" source="b761" target="SNOMED_CT:282716004" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b761 SNOMED CT 282716004 = ICF b761 Spontaneous movements functions: the involuntary,
        non-goal-directed, automatic body functions underlying spontaneous general and specific
        movements (e.g. infant general movements, automatic fidgety/spontaneous motor output). Target =,
        active RF2 production 20260701. No dedicated function-observable exists in the mirror — SNOMED CT
        models spontaneous movement output only indirectly (88828000 is cortical, not motor;
        general-movement assessment is captured in paediatric scales, not a function observable).
        Related (weak): 282716004 gross motor functions is clinically associated with the
        spontaneous-movement output (gross/general spontaneous movements are a subset of gross motor
        function) but is not an ancestor, descendant, or component of the ICF
        spontaneous-movement-FUNCTION framing — it is a coarse, function-framed observable that overlaps
        the source domain without subsuming it. Recorded as a lead for a reviewer, not asserted as a
        mapping; the association is loose. mapping_type=related.
        """
}
mapping "b7610.1" source="b7610" target="SNOMED_CT:282716004" relationship=related_to effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b7610 SNOMED CT 282716004 = ICF b7610 General movements: the specific function of general
        (whole-body) spontaneous movements — the gross/general spontaneous motor output (e.g. the infant
        general movements of Prechtl's assessment), a child of b761. Target =, active RF2 production
        20260701. No dedicated function-observable exists in the mirror — Prechtl's general-movement
        assessment is captured observationally, not as a function concept, and 707621005 is a scale, not
        a function observable. Related (weak): 282716004 gross motor functions is clinically associated
        with the whole-body general-movements output but is not equivalent (general movements are an
        involuntary-spontaneous phenomenon; gross motor functions denote the broader voluntary +
        involuntary gross-motor class), so the link is a loose reviewer lead. mapping_type=related.
        """
}
