        function. (2) SNOMED CT 44515000 =, active RF2 production 20260701 — covers the perseveration axis;
        SNOMED CT frames perseveration primarily as a cognitive/behavioural finding rather than a motor
        function. Partial (low): target captures the perseveration component but leaves the stereotypy
        axis uncovered, and the finding framing is partly outside ICF's motor-function framing. Each
        target carries its own type/confidence; order strongest-first. mapping_type=partial for each.
        """
}
